# Manual file-copy backups (_pre_<change>.ext) — git is the version history
# now; these predate git in this repo and shouldn't keep growing inside it.
# NOTE: 118 pre-existing _pre_* files are already baked into the F0 commit
# (33f2bd1) since this pattern wasn't excluded yet at that point — un-bloating
# those would need a history rewrite, not done here. This only stops NEW ones.
*_pre_*
# The pattern above needs a LITERAL "_pre_", so every suffix where a word
# runs straight on from "_pre" slipped through — _precontaminationfix_,
# _prelookupflag_, _preocrfullimage_, _preocrsetcode_, _preeragate_,
# _predbretry_, _prepreloadcheck_, _preuploadguidance_, _preuploadguide_.
# Each needed its own rule, added one task at a time, five weeks running.
#
# Replaced 2026-08-04 by the general form below. Verified against the repo
# at that date: catches 13/13 existing backup files, and matches 0 of 529
# tracked files. The trailing _2026 anchors it to the dated-backup naming
# convention, so ordinary sources (prepare_2026.py, report_2026.md) do not
# match — the "_pre" and the date must BOTH be present.
*_pre*_2026*

