# Rescued scan query images (2026-08-02) - 593 MiB of binaries.
# Verified copies live at C:\MatchIT\eval_rescue\ and
# C:\Users\c_a_b\grailsweep-backups\. Deliberately NOT in git:
# binaries bloat history permanently and are already backed up twice.
# MANIFEST.txt IS tracked - it is the durable record of the set.
eval_rescue/**/*.jpg

# Labelling tool artifacts (2026-08-02). Both are regenerable from
# C:\CardsDB + set_metadata.json + set_dates.json. label.html carries a
# 6.9 MiB inline index; lookup_index.json is 22 MiB. Neither belongs in
# history. images_shuffled.json IS tracked - it is the record of the
# blind shuffle order and cannot be reproduced from the seed alone.
eval_rescue/labelling/lookup_index.json
eval_rescue/labelling/label.html
eval_rescue/labelling/backup_prelookup_20260802/

# ============================================
# Node / TypeScript (added 2026-08-08 — auth-engine/ brought Node
# dependencies into the tree for the first time)
# ============================================
# auth-engine/node_modules/ alone was 267 untracked files with no rule
# catching it before this. node_modules is always regenerable from
# package.json/package-lock.json, so it never belongs in history.
node_modules/
# tsc build output — regenerable from the .ts sources via `npm run build`.
dist/
build/
# Next.js build cache — not used yet, but excluded pre-emptively so a
# future Next app in this repo doesn't repeat the node_modules gap.
.next/
# Incremental compile cache tsc writes next to tsconfig.json — local
# build-speed state, not source.
*.tsbuildinfo
# auth-engine/*.js compiled from same-named .ts sources (tsc, no outDir
# set, so output lands next to the source) — regenerable, not source.
# Listed explicitly by name rather than a blanket auth-engine/*.js
# rule: registry.test.js is hand-written with no .ts sibling, and a
# wildcard would silently swallow it (and any future hand-written JS).
auth-engine/authEngine.js
auth-engine/authEngineBrowser.js
auth-engine/authFunction.js
auth-engine/authWorker.js
auth-engine/imageHooks.js
auth-engine/index.js
# 8 one-off discovery scripts written to locate auth-engine wiring points
# during the 2026-08-08 build. Classified as scratch, not durable tooling.
# Kept on disk, out of history — consistent with the _pre_* lesson recorded
# above.
tools/

# Point-in-time backups taken before destructive set_metadata.json
# operations during the 2026-08-10 JP set-metadata merge (already covered
# by *_pre_* above, listed explicitly for clarity) and the merged-output
# file staged for upload. Kept on disk, not history — the live copy is on
# the Modal volume.
set_metadata_pre_*.json
set_metadata_volume_merged.json
# Scratch diff/verification output from the same 2026-08-10 merge — disposable
# analysis artifacts, not durable tooling or data.
diff_report.txt
set_metadata_postupload_verify.json

# images.db copies pulled down during the 2026-08-10 incident diagnosis/
# restore (backup diff, post-restore verification). ~550MB each — must
# never be committed. Kept on disk, not history.
backup_check.db
restore_verify.db
volume_images_check.db
images_volume_corrupt.db

# scheduler_log.json snapshot pulled from the volume during the 2026-08-11
# scheduled-job cadence recon — a point-in-time production data dump, not
# source. Kept on disk, not history.
scheduler_log_check.json

# JP SWSH SKU-link output (2026-08-23) — regenerable from the committed
# jp_cardid_maps/ + identifier_lookup.json via `python link_jp_skus.py`.
# jp_sku_links.json's content also depends on which --sets filter was last
# passed (a full run overwrites it with every set, not just these 7), so a
# committed copy would misrepresent itself as a definitive, complete link
# set. Kept on disk, not history.
jp_sku_links.json
jp_sku_links_report.txt

# One-off image_id list built for a single scoped upload_new_images_by_id.py
# run (2026-08-23 JP SWSH ingest) — regenerable via a one-line SQL query
# against images.db, not source data. Kept on disk, not history.
jp_swsh_7sets_image_ids.json

# scratch/ — debug crops, OCR spot-checks, and one-off investigation scripts
# accumulated across sessions while building the JP SWSH OCR pipeline. Not
# referenced at runtime; disposable by the same convention as tools/ above
# (reusable pieces get promoted out, e.g. check_row_count.py on 2026-08-23).
scratch/
